  <content>
    <description>
      <levelledPara id="par-0001"><title>General</title>
        <para>The seat recline actuator is a mechanical lockable spring strut. It holds the seat back at the selected recline angle and returns it to upright when released. Part numbers RA-7100-01 and RA-7100-02 (after SB 25-0012).</para>
        <figure id="fig-0001"><title>Seat recline actuator</title><graphic infoEntityIdent="ICN-ASTDEMO-A-252171-C-ZZD01-00001-A-001-01"/></figure>
      </levelledPara>
      <levelledPara id="par-0002"><title>Main parts</title>
        <para>The actuator has these main parts:</para>
        <para><randomList>
          <listItem><para>A housing (10) which contains a piston rod (20) sealed by two packings (110).</para></listItem>
          <listItem><para>A compression spring (50, or 50A after SB 25-0012) which pushes the piston rod to the extended position.</para></listItem>
          <listItem><para>A lock mechanism (60) with a release lever (70) and a lock pin (80), attached by four screws (90) and washers (100).</para></listItem>
          <listItem><para>A threaded rod end (30) with a bushing (120), held by a self-locking nut (40).</para></listItem>
        </randomList></para>
      </levelledPara>
      <levelledPara id="par-0003"><title>Operation</title>
        <para>When the release lever is pulled, the lock pin disengages and the piston rod can move. Full stroke is 75 mm (2.95 in).</para>
      </levelledPara>
    </description>
